Building a Right to Erasure Workflow in PostgreSQL
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Design a multi-table PostgreSQL schema representing user data across a system
Build a Python service that traces all records tied to a data subject
Implement a soft-delete then hard-delete pattern with audit logging
Simulate backup anonymization to satisfy GDPR Article 17 across all data copies
Generate an erasure confirmation certificate
Prerequisites
Basic SQL (JOINs, foreign keys, transactions)
Basic Python (functions, classes, psycopg2 or similar)
Familiarity with GDPR Article 17 concepts (right to erasure)
Comfort with Linux terminal
Environment Setup
