Troubleshooting
Foreign key violation on delete: Ensure you delete from orders/support_tickets before deleting from users.
Connection refused: Check sudo systemctl status postgresql and confirm pg_hba.conf allows local password auth.
Transaction left open: Always call conn.commit() on success and conn.rollback() in an except block.
Conclusion
In this lab, you built a functional right-to-erasure workflow in PostgreSQL that mirrors real-world GDPR Article 17 obligations. You designed a multi-table dataset, wrote a Python service to trace personal data across tables, implemented a two-stage soft-delete/hard-delete process with a full audit trail, anonymized backup copies of user data, and produced a data-subject-facing erasure certificate. These skills directly support Backend Engineer and Privacy Engineer roles and align with IAPP CIPT competencies in privacy-by-design implementation.
